    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ec25d88_7e3912f3",
        "filename": "common/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1324172
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-14T03:30:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see no point into putting into different variable. First, we save stack memory. Second, we \u0027destroy\u0027 pre-hashed value so in case of any issues it is less likely to leak. If just to create another pointer named authTimeSecretHash, but pointing to same place - it will be more confusing.\n\nAs for naming - i don\u0027t think adding \u0027Hash\u0027 will make it clear. From cr50 standpoint is doesn\u0027t matter what it is - it is some 32-byte \u0027secret\u0027. We don\u0027t add any semantic here except that we know that we need to compute SHA256 of this value prior to use in U2F_sign.",
